 ETH eth1 → rh1 (gas) | 1000000000000000 | 833333333333333 ETH | $1.40 |\n| 3 | q_4 | Bridge WBTC eth1 → rh1 | 247500 | 246666 | $1.4004 |\n| 4 | q_6 | rh1: swap WBTC → ETH | 246666 | 49233200000000000 ETH | $0.36 |\n| 5 | q_3 | Bridge ETH eth1 → arb1 (gas) | 1000000000000000 | 833333333333333 ETH | $1.40 |\n| 6 | q_5 | Bridge WBTC eth1 → arb1 | 247500 | 246666 | $1.4004 |\n| 7 | q_7 | arb1: swap WBTC → USDC | 246666 | 147699600 USDC units | $0.36 |\n\nWhy these legs:\n- **Gas bridges (q_2, q_3):** rh1 and arb1 both have 0 ETH, so neither could pay for its swap. arb1 also needs ETH left over for one more transaction because it will end up holding USDC. A bridge of 0.00004–0.00006 ETH is too small to cover the fee, so each gas bridge sends 0.001 ETH.\n- **USDC route:** bridging WBTC to Arbitrum and swapping there costs $1.76. Swapping to USDC on mainnet and bridging the USDC would cost $5.30 and give less USDC (145500000 instead of 147699600).\n\nExpected balances at the end:\n- **eth1:** about 0.0465 ETH, 0 WBTC.\n- **rh1:** about 0.04406 ETH (more than its gas reserve).\n- **arb1:** about 147.7 USDC and about 0.00081 ETH for gas.\n\nCaveats:\n- If the first swap returns a different WBTC amount than 495000, I'll quote the halves again before bridging.\n- Quotes expire after 300 s, and the whole route takes about 4–5 minutes, so some legs will probably need new quotes partway through.\n\nReply **approve** to run it, **reject** to stop, or give me a lower cost cap."}]},{"role":"user","sequence":22,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, go ahead with that plan."}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":23,"content":[{"type":"toolCall","name":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_execute_leg","arguments":{"quote_id":"q_1","approval_id":"appr_9"},"id":"toolu_01U76r6hRmzeL2R2pEFW3XGe"}]},{"role":"tool","sequence":24,"content":[{"type":"toolResult","text":"{\"tx_id\":\"tx_10\"}","toolCallId":"toolu_01U76r6hRmzeL2R2pEFW3XGe","toolName":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_execute_leg","isError":false}